domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"e16932c4-3dc5-4235-a976-c87da064c7f4"}],"viewed_images":{},"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/2e374cfc-9fcf-40cf-90e7-e408c3a6d1a4/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/2e374cfc-9fcf-40cf-90e7-e408c3a6d1a4/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/2e374cfc-9fcf-40cf-90e7-e408c3a6d1a4/user-data/outputs"},"raw_messages":[{"content":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"65984f46-c5c1-4d9a-ab7c-f5aec379050e"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\nScene skill filter result: SkillRouter ranking is disabled. Detected scene(s): network_traffic. The listed custom/domain skills are all enabled skills for the detected scene. Treat them as an allowed candidate set, choose the specific matching skill or skills for the task, and then load only the chosen skill file(s). Public skills from the base prompt remain available.\nTask: 请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。\n\n**Current Available Skills:**\n- The current <available_skills> list is empty.\n- No routed custom/domain skill matched this turn.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"e16932c4-3dc5-4235-a976-c87da064c7f4"}],"artifacts":[],"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","normalized_query":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","routing_query":"场景：网络流量。场景ID：network_traffic。场景说明：网络流量、PCAP、会话、协议、异常通信、恶意流量、网络安全事件分析场景。需要识别参数：分析对象、分析目标、输出形式。用户原始问题：我将根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把网络流量场景中的事件分为自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类","scene":"network_traffic","scene_name":"网络流量","params":{"分析对象":"事件","分析目标":"按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["network_traffic"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_3f9ec6","text":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_c8c5ff","text":"读取网络流量场景中的安全告警事件数据源，解析数据结构，定位并提取告警置信度（如评分值或模型概率）、证据完整性（如PCAP抓包数量、日志关联深度、会话状态记录）及潜在影响（如目标资产重要性、暴露面范围、敏感数据标识）等核心字段。"},{"task_span_id":"span_cf95a4","text":"结合网络安全事件处置规范，构建三级分类判定逻辑与判断口径，明确各维度阈值及组合规则，例如设定高置信度加完整证据链加低风险触发自动通过，中高置信度加证据缺口或高风险触发优先复核，其余情形归入需要人工复核。"},{"task_span_id":"span_b2d64c","text":"将解析后的事件指标代入判定规则进行逐项匹配与交叉评估，计算综合分类结果，输出带有分类标签、关键指标快照及规则命中详情的阶段性结构化结果集。"},{"task_span_id":"span_ba0b4c","text":"对分类结果进行聚合校验与格式规范化，生成可溯源的分类明细清单，附带各类别事件的数量分布、典型样本特征描述及差异化处置流转建议，完成最终交付物封装。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_414db3","scene":"network_traffic","scene_name":"网络流量","text":"我将根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把网络流量场景中的事件分为自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","params":{"分析对象":"事件","分析目标":"按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_414db3","scene":"network_traffic","scene_name":"网络流量","text":"我将根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把网络流量场景中的事件分为自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","params":{"分析对象":"事件","分析目标":"按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：分析对象。需要分析的网络流量文件、数据集或场景名称，如 pcap、pcapng、Neris、DNS、HTTP、TLS、会话日志等","提取可选参数：分析目标。用户希望识别、统计或总结的目标，如异常通信、恶意流量、协议分布、主机行为、IOC、攻击链等","提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的结果形式，如 summary、报告、表格、图表、证据清单等"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:65984f46-c5c1-4d9a-ab7c-f5aec379050e"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":false,"primary_goal":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","scene":"network_traffic","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":[],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":0.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":[],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:65984f46-c5c1-4d9a-ab7c-f5aec379050e"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_ids":[],"allowed_tool_names":[]}

event: values
data: {"messages":[{"content":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"65984f46-c5c1-4d9a-ab7c-f5aec379050e"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\nScene skill filter result: SkillRouter ranking is disabled. Detected scene(s): network_traffic. The listed custom/domain skills are all enabled skills for the detected scene. Treat them as an allowed candidate set, choose the specific matching skill or skills for the task, and then load only the chosen skill file(s). Public skills from the base prompt remain available.\nTask: 请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。\n\n**Current Available Skills:**\n- The current <available_skills> list is empty.\n- No routed custom/domain skill matched this turn.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"e16932c4-3dc5-4235-a976-c87da064c7f4"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：网络流量。场景ID：network_traffic\n识别场景：网络流量 (network_traffic)；场景模式：single；候选场景：network_traffic\n任务切分：\n- 请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取网络流量场景中的安全告警事件数据源，解析数据结构，定位并提取告警置信度（如评分值或模型概率）、证据完整性（如PCAP抓包数量、日志关联深度、会话状态记录）及潜在影响（如目标资产重要性、暴露面范围、敏感数据标识）等核心字段。\n2. 结合网络安全事件处置规范，构建三级分类判定逻辑与判断口径，明确各维度阈值及组合规则，例如设定高置信度加完整证据链加低风险触发自动通过，中高置信度加证据缺口或高风险触发优先复核，其余情形归入需要人工复核。\n3. 将解析后的事件指标代入判定规则进行逐项匹配与交叉评估，计算综合分类结果，输出带有分类标签、关键指标快照及规则命中详情的阶段性结构化结果集。\n4. 对分类结果进行聚合校验与格式规范化，生成可溯源的分类明细清单，附带各类别事件的数量分布、典型样本特征描述及差异化处置流转建议，完成最终交付物封装。\n场景任务：\n- network_traffic: 我将根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把网络流量场景中的事件分为自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。；参数：{'分析对象': '事件', '分析目标': '按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类'}\n已提取参数：{'分析对象': '事件', '分析目标': '按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：分析对象。需要分析的网络流量文件、数据集或场景名称，如 pcap、pcapng、Neris、DNS、HTTP、TLS、会话日志等\n- 提取可选参数：分析目标。用户希望识别、统计或总结的目标，如异常通信、恶意流量、协议分布、主机行为、IOC、攻击链等\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的结果形式，如 summary、报告、表格、图表、证据清单等\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"55cffa25-4bdd-4985-87bd-88d40214fdbc"}],"viewed_images":{},"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/2e374cfc-9fcf-40cf-90e7-e408c3a6d1a4/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/2e374cfc-9fcf-40cf-90e7-e408c3a6d1a4/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/2e374cfc-9fcf-40cf-90e7-e408c3a6d1a4/user-data/outputs"},"raw_messages":[{"content":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"65984f46-c5c1-4d9a-ab7c-f5aec379050e"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\nScene skill filter result: SkillRouter ranking is disabled. Detected scene(s): network_traffic. The listed custom/domain skills are all enabled skills for the detected scene. Treat them as an allowed candidate set, choose the specific matching skill or skills for the task, and then load only the chosen skill file(s). Public skills from the base prompt remain available.\nTask: 请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。\n\n**Current Available Skills:**\n- The current <available_skills> list is empty.\n- No routed custom/domain skill matched this turn.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"e16932c4-3dc5-4235-a976-c87da064c7f4"}],"artifacts":[],"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","normalized_query":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","routing_query":"场景：网络流量。场景ID：network_traffic。场景说明：网络流量、PCAP、会话、协议、异常通信、恶意流量、网络安全事件分析场景。需要识别参数：分析对象、分析目标、输出形式。用户原始问题：我将根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把网络流量场景中的事件分为自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类","scene":"network_traffic","scene_name":"网络流量","params":{"分析对象":"事件","分析目标":"按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["network_traffic"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_3f9ec6","text":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_c8c5ff","text":"读取网络流量场景中的安全告警事件数据源，解析数据结构，定位并提取告警置信度（如评分值或模型概率）、证据完整性（如PCAP抓包数量、日志关联深度、会话状态记录）及潜在影响（如目标资产重要性、暴露面范围、敏感数据标识）等核心字段。"},{"task_span_id":"span_cf95a4","text":"结合网络安全事件处置规范，构建三级分类判定逻辑与判断口径，明确各维度阈值及组合规则，例如设定高置信度加完整证据链加低风险触发自动通过，中高置信度加证据缺口或高风险触发优先复核，其余情形归入需要人工复核。"},{"task_span_id":"span_b2d64c","text":"将解析后的事件指标代入判定规则进行逐项匹配与交叉评估，计算综合分类结果，输出带有分类标签、关键指标快照及规则命中详情的阶段性结构化结果集。"},{"task_span_id":"span_ba0b4c","text":"对分类结果进行聚合校验与格式规范化，生成可溯源的分类明细清单，附带各类别事件的数量分布、典型样本特征描述及差异化处置流转建议，完成最终交付物封装。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_414db3","scene":"network_traffic","scene_name":"网络流量","text":"我将根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把网络流量场景中的事件分为自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","params":{"分析对象":"事件","分析目标":"按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_414db3","scene":"network_traffic","scene_name":"网络流量","text":"我将根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把网络流量场景中的事件分为自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","params":{"分析对象":"事件","分析目标":"按告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响分级分类"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：分析对象。需要分析的网络流量文件、数据集或场景名称，如 pcap、pcapng、Neris、DNS、HTTP、TLS、会话日志等","提取可选参数：分析目标。用户希望识别、统计或总结的目标，如异常通信、恶意流量、协议分布、主机行为、IOC、攻击链等","提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的结果形式，如 summary、报告、表格、图表、证据清单等"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:65984f46-c5c1-4d9a-ab7c-f5aec379050e"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":false,"primary_goal":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请根据告警置信度、证据完整性和潜在影响，把事件分成自动通过、需要人工复核和优先复核三类。","scene":"network_traffic","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":[],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":0.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":[],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:65984f46-c5c1-4d9a-ab7c-f5aec379050e"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_i