ponse_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":182,"prompt_tokens":11974,"total_tokens":12156,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":66,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":182},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":11974}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-f245c5e2-74c3-9378-82f3-ffa757f7194b","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9e5f-be4e-7803-b9c8-50d88d0cbdbd-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取network-traffic数据集的字段映射和说明文档","path":"/mnt/datasets/network-traffic/schema/field_mapping.yaml"},"id":"call_24bd7affc76248e793b51960","type":"tool_call"},{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取network-traffic数据集的README说明","path":"/mnt/datasets/network-traffic/schema/README.md"},"id":"call_0658d6d5e2844833895a5695","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":11974,"output_tokens":182,"total_tokens":12156,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":66}}},{"content":"canonical_fields:\n  timestamp:\n    - timestamp\n    - ts\n    - time\n    - event_time\n    - start_time\n    - flow_start\n    - first_seen\n  end_time:\n    - end_time\n    - end_timestamp\n    - flow_end\n    - last_seen\n  relative_time_s:\n    - relative_time_s\n    - time_relative_s\n    - frame.time_relative\n  start_relative_time_s:\n    - start_relative_time_s\n    - flow_start_relative_s\n    - relative_start_time_s\n  end_relative_time_s:\n    - end_relative_time_s\n    - flow_end_relative_s\n    - relative_end_time_s\n  time_is_relative:\n    - time_is_relative\n    - uses_relative_time\n    - relative_time_flag\n  src_ip:\n    - src_ip\n    - source_ip\n    - src\n    - sip\n    - src_addr\n    - source_address\n  dst_ip:\n    - dst_ip\n    - destination_ip\n    - dest_ip\n    - dst\n    - dip\n    - dst_addr\n    - destination_address\n  src_port:\n    - src_port\n    - source_port\n    - sport\n    - l4_src_port\n  dst_port:\n    - dst_port\n    - destination_port\n    - dest_port\n    - dport\n    - l4_dst_port\n  protocol:\n    - protocol\n    - proto\n    - l4_proto\n    - transport\n  app_protocol:\n    - app_protocol\n    - application_protocol\n    - app_proto\n    - l7_proto\n  service:\n    - service\n    - app_service\n    - destination_service\n  bytes:\n    - bytes\n    - byte_count\n    - bytes_total\n    - total_bytes\n    - octets\n    - in_bytes\n  packets:\n    - packets\n    - packet_count\n    - total_packets\n    - pkts\n  flow_duration:\n    - flow_duration\n    - duration\n    - session_duration\n    - elapsed_ms\n  duration_ms:\n    - duration_ms\n    - elapsed_ms\n    - duration_millis\n    - session_duration_ms\n  session_state:\n    - session_state\n    - state\n    - connection_state\n    - flow_state\n  rule_name:\n    - rule_name\n    - rule\n    - policy_rule\n    - detection_rule\n  tcp_flags:\n    - tcp_flags\n    - tcp_flags_seen\n    - flags\n  dns_query:\n    - dns_query\n    - dns_qname\n    - query_name\n    - domain\n  tls_sni:\n    - tls_sni\n    - sni\n    - server_name\n    - tls_server_name\n  http_host:\n    - http_host\n    - host\n    - http_hostname\n  direction:\n    - direction\n    - traffic_direction\n    - flow_direction\n  action:\n    - action\n    - status\n    - outcome\n    - verdict\n    - decision\n  flow_start_reason:\n    - flow_start_reason\n    - session_start_reason\n    - start_reason\n  flow_end_reason:\n    - flow_end_reason\n    - session_end_reason\n    - end_reason\n  asset_id:\n    - asset_id\n    - host_id\n    - endpoint_id\n  user_id:\n    - user_id\n    - username\n    - account_id\n  device_id:\n    - device_id\n    - appliance_id\n    - sensor_device_id\n  sensor_id:\n    - sensor_id\n    - probe_id\n    - sensor\n  dataset_label:\n    - dataset_label\n    - dataset\n    - dataset_name\n  traffic_family:\n    - traffic_family\n    - traffic_type\n    - family\ndefault_metrics:\n  - count\n  - sum:bytes\n  - sum:packets\n  - avg:flow_duration\nprofiles:\n  wireshark_packet:\n    canonical_fields:\n      timestamp:\n        - frame.time_epoch\n        - frame.time\n        - frame.time_relative\n      src_ip:\n        - ip.src\n        - ipv6.src\n      dst_ip:\n        - ip.dst\n        - ipv6.dst\n      src_port:\n        - tcp.srcport\n        - udp.srcport\n      dst_port:\n        - tcp.dstport\n        - udp.dstport\n      protocol:\n        - _ws.col.Protocol\n        - frame.protocols\n        - ip.proto\n      frame_len:\n        - frame.len\n      payload_bytes:\n        - tcp.len\n        - udp.length\n        - ip.len\n      tcp_flags:\n        - tcp.flags.str\n        - tcp.flags\n      ttl:\n        - ip.ttl\n        - ipv6.hlim\n      ip_version:\n        - ip.version\n      icmp_type:\n        - icmp.type\n      icmp_code:\n        - icmp.code\n      dns_query:\n        - dns.qry.name\n      tls_sni:\n        - tls.handshake.extensions_server_name\n      http_host:\n        - http.host\n      mac_src:\n        - eth.src\n      mac_dst:\n        - eth.dst\nnotes:\n  - \"Add aliases here when a new vendor or export format uses different column names.\"\n  - \"Canonical fields are used to build the unified 'flows' view for network-traffic-analysis.\"\n  - \"Profiles let the script auto-detect common export formats such as Wireshark/tshark without rewriting source columns.\"\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"aceb7fb7-5375-465b-a6ae-56243954872f","tool_call_id":"call_24bd7affc76248e793b51960","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"# Network Traffic Dataset Schema\n\nThis folder stores local, tracked configuration for the network traffic analysis workflow.\n\nFiles:\n\n- `field_mapping.yaml`: canonical field aliases used by the skill script\n  - supports shared aliases plus source-specific profiles such as `wireshark_packet`\n\nRecommended raw dataset shape:\n\n- One row per flow, session, alert, or request log\n- Prefer at least these columns when available:\n  - `timestamp` or relative-time fields such as `relative_time_s` / `start_relative_time_s`\n  - `src_ip`\n  - `dst_ip`\n  - `src_port`\n  - `dst_port`\n  - `protocol`\n  - `bytes`\n  - `packets`\n  - `flow_duration`\n  - `direction`\n  - `action`\n\nSupported input formats in phase 1:\n\n- `.csv`\n- `.parquet`\n- `.json`\n- `.jsonl`\n- `.xlsx`\n- `.xls`\n\nMapping behavior:\n\n- Source files keep their original columns.\n- The analysis script builds a canonical `flows` view for downstream actions.\n- Common vendor/export aliases can be added to `field_mapping.yaml`.\n- Source-specific profiles can be auto-detected without breaking older datasets.\n- Time-aware analysis supports both:\n  - absolute timestamps via `timestamp` / `end_time`\n  - relative capture time via `relative_time_s`, `start_relative_time_s`, `end_relative_time_s`, and `time_is_relative`\n\nPCAP preprocessing output fields:\n\n- `packet.csv` always includes the existing core fields plus:\n  - `relative_time_s`\n  - `time_is_relative`\n  - `app_protocol`\n  - `service`\n  - `ip_version`\n  - `frame_len`\n  - `ttl`\n  - `payload_bytes`\n  - `tcp_flags`\n  - `dns_query`\n  - `tls_sni`\n  - `http_host`\n  - `icmp_type`\n  - `icmp_code`\n  - `flow_id`\n  - `packet_count`\n  - `byte_count`\n  - `bytes_total`\n  - `src_bytes`\n  - `dst_bytes`\n  - `src_packets`\n  - `dst_packets`\n  - `duration_ms`\n  - `session_state`\n  - `rule_name`\n  - `device_id`\n  - `sensor_id`\n  - `vlan_id`\n  - `src_zone`\n  - `dst_zone`\n  - `src_asset_group`\n  - `dst_asset_group`\n  - `nat_src_ip`\n  - `nat_dst_ip`\n  - `dst_asn`\n  - `dst_country`\n  - `asset_id`\n  - `user_id`\n  - `dataset_label`\n  - `traffic_family`\n  - `pcap_name`\n  - `mac_src`\n  - `mac_dst`\n- `flow.csv` always includes the existing core fields plus:\n  - `end_time`\n  - `start_relative_time_s`\n  - `end_relative_time_s`\n  - `time_is_relative`\n  - `app_protocol`\n  - `service`\n  - `session_state`\n  - `flow_start_reason`\n  - `flow_end_reason`\n  - `rule_name`\n  - `tcp_flags`\n  - `ip_version`\n  - `bytes_total`\n  - `packet_count`\n  - `payload_bytes`\n  - `src_bytes`\n  - `dst_bytes`\n  - `src_packets`\n  - `dst_packets`\n  - `vlan_id`\n  - `src_zone`\n  - `dst_zone`\n  - `src_asset_group`\n  - `dst_asset_group`\n  - `nat_src_ip`\n  - `nat_dst_ip`\n  - `dst_asn`\n  - `dst_country`\n  - `dns_query`\n  - `tls_sni`\n  - `http_host`\n  - `asset_id`\n  - `user_id`\n  - `duration`\n  - `duration_ms`\n  - `flow_id`\n  - `tcp_flags_seen`\n  - `ttl_min`\n  - `ttl_max`\n  - `ttl_avg`\n  - `icmp_type`\n  - `icmp_code`\n  - `device_id`\n  - `sensor_id`\n  - `dataset_label`\n  - `traffic_family`\n\nFlow semantics:\n\n- `flow.csv` is now session-oriented rather than coarse conversation-oriented.\n- TCP flows are split using:\n  - SYN-preferring session starts\n  - FIN / RST termination\n  - idle timeout boundaries\n- Non-TCP flows are split using idle timeout boundaries.\n- Relative-time captures keep their time offsets in dedicated fields instead of being rewritten as `1970-01-01...` timestamps.\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"a05dae4d-8cfb-43f5-9b6e-3ecfc96af7fa","tool_call_id":"call_0658d6d5e2844833895a5695","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":270,"prompt_tokens":14393,"total_tokens":14663,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":197,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":270},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":14393}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-68c2fb32-5c77-9510-a7f2-a7